cua-driver-rs 0.14.2 installed.


Next steps:

  1. Try it:
       /Users/runner/.local/bin/cua-driver --version
       /Users/runner/.local/bin/cua-driver list-tools

  2. Grant permissions (macOS — Accessibility + Screen Recording):
       /Users/runner/.local/bin/cua-driver permissions status   # report status (read-only; tells you which
                                       # identity the grants belong to)
       /Users/runner/.local/bin/cua-driver permissions grant    # the correct way to grant — launches the installed
                                       # app so every dialog and Settings entry matches
                                       # this driver identity, not your terminal.
                                   # Tip: `--autostart` (above) keeps a launchd daemon
                                   # running so you grant once and it persists.

  3. Agent skill pack (optional):
       /Users/runner/.local/bin/cua-driver skills install   # fetch + link the cua-driver skill pack
                                   # into Claude Code / Codex / OpenClaw / OpenCode.
                                   # The install never touches your agent dirs.

  4. As an MCP server — run the one matching your client. Each is also
     available via '/Users/runner/.local/bin/cua-driver mcp-config --client <name>':

     • Claude Code (computer-use compatibility mode):
         /Users/runner/.local/bin/cua-driver mcp-config --client claude
       Copy-paste the printed command into your shell — it uses
       `claude mcp add-json` (not bare `--`) so the long flag travels
       through PowerShell's arg parser intact. This mode grounds Claude
       Code's vision/computer-use-style flow on CuaDriver window
       screenshots — it keeps the normal CuaDriver tools and changes
       only the screenshot tool.

     • Codex (OpenAI):
         codex mcp add cua-driver -- /Users/runner/.local/bin/cua-driver mcp

     • Qwen Code:
         qwen mcp add cua-driver /Users/runner/.local/bin/cua-driver mcp

     • Factory Droid:
         droid mcp add cua-driver "/Users/runner/.local/bin/cua-driver mcp"

     • OpenClaw:
         /Users/runner/.local/bin/cua-driver mcp-config --client openclaw

     • GitHub Copilot CLI (paste into ~/.copilot/mcp-config.json):
         {
           "mcpServers": {
             "cua-driver": {
               "type": "local",
               "command": "/Users/runner/.local/bin/cua-driver",
               "args": ["mcp"],
               "tools": ["*"]
             }
